      "content": "thanks for that. i've been reading a lot of articles online lately and it feels like most experts and urban planners are basically saying that high-density is the only way to actually fix the housing problem and that the single-family stuff is just holding the city back. is there actually any real evidence or logical argument for the single-family side, or is it mostly just people trying to stop change?",
